  "title": "Acute Tbr1 loss drives a small cortical projection-neuron synaptic/membrane program without reactivating neonatal layer-6 fate targets",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Tbr1 was FDR-active in cortical and projection-like glutamatergic classes with recurrent Cpne6 up-regulation and Dkk3 or Epb41/Nptx1 decreases; NP-CT-L6b-OB Glut instead showed an all-up response including Cacna1g, Cpne6, Gaa, and C1qtnf4.",
  "biological_interpretation": "TBR1 retains a mature, context-specific cortical synaptic/membrane regulon that is separable from neonatal layer-6 target wiring and from silent T-box paralogs.",
